# Line endings are normalised to LF in the repository. Windows checkouts still get
# CRLF in the working tree for editing; only what git stores is forced to LF, so a
# file edited on Windows and a file edited on the cluster no longer show up as a
# whole-file diff against each other.
* text=auto

# Anything the cluster executes must be LF in the working tree as well: a stray CR
# makes bash fail with an unreadable "\r: command not found".
*.sh      text eol=lf
*.sbatch  text eol=lf
init.sh   text eol=lf

*.png  binary
*.jpg  binary
*.pdf  binary
*.pkl  binary
*.parquet binary
